{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeFubini","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeFubini","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronRegion","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Constructions.Pi","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Prod"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_of_subset_disk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_of_subset_disk","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L283-L289","doc":"The pointwise corollary, for a base in the OPEN disk. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_of_ae_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney_of_ae_lt","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L264-L281","doc":"**H4-2 — the Fubini reduction, in the form H4-3 will consume.**\n\n    Vol(chimney T R)  =  ∫∫_T  dA / (2(R² − x² − y²)).\n\nThe hypothesis is **almost-everywhere**, and that is not a technical\ngeneralisation — it is what makes the statement applicable at all.  Milnor's\nbase triangle is *inscribed* in the circle, so its three VERTICES lie exactly\nON it, where `R² − x² − y² = 0` and the fibre mass is `⊤` (`fibreMass_eq_top`).\nA pointwise `∀ w ∈ T` hypothesis would therefore exclude the closed triangle —\nprecisely the case H4-3 needs.  The vertices are a null set, so a.e. is both\nsufficient and honest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.fibreMass_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.fibreMass_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L209-L257","doc":"**Off the open disk the fibre carries infinite mass.**\n\n`Real.sqrt` of a non-positive number is `0`, so the chimney's floor degenerates\nto `z > 0` and `∫_0^∞ dz/z³` diverges.  Proved rather than asserted, because it\nis what makes `hypVolume_chimney_of_subset_disk`'s hypothesis the exact\nboundary between a finite and an infinite volume, not a convenience. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.fibreMass_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.fibreMass_eq","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L181-L205","doc":"**H4-2b — the fibre mass over a base point strictly inside the circle.**\n\n`∫_{√(R²−d²)}^{∞} dz/z³ = 1/(2(R²−d²))`, now as an `ℝ≥0∞` mass.  This is H4-1's\nvalue, transported across the `∫⁻`/`∫` boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.hypVolume_chimney","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L116-L172","doc":"**H4-2a (Fubini) — a chimney's hyperbolic volume is the base integral of\nits fibre masses.**\n\nUnconditional: no assumption that the base lies inside the disk, so both sides\nare permitted to be `⊤` (and by `fibreMass_eq_top` they are, as soon as the base\nmeets the exterior of the circle). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.fibreMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.fibreMass","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L106-L109","doc":"**The hyperbolic mass of one vertical fibre** over the base point `w`, above\nthe radius-`R` hemisphere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurePreserving_splitEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.measurePreserving_splitEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L93-L99","doc":"The split is measure-preserving: Lebesgue on `Fin 3 → ℝ` goes to Lebesgue\non `ℝ × (ℝ × ℝ)`.  Both halves are standard. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv_symm_apply_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv_symm_apply_two","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L90-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv_symm_apply_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv_symm_apply_one","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L87-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv_symm_apply_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv_symm_apply_zero","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L84-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolume.splitEquiv","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicVolumeFubini.lean#L78-L82","doc":"**`Fin 3 → ℝ ≃ᵐ ℝ × (ℝ × ℝ)`, height first.**  Splits coordinate `2` off\nthe Pi type, then pairs the remaining two. ","signatureChunk":0}]}